  "findings": [
    "The pair scanner does not exhaust all permutation cycles. A three-cycle recurrent matrix with constant input/readout columns has a cyclic automorphism and no transposition automorphism.",
    "Positive gauge D transforms Wi,Wh,Wo as DWi,DWhD^-1,WoD^-1; Euclidean augmented-row cosines are not invariant. Exact collinearity and near-collinearity scores are distinct.",
    "SVD row projection keeps Wo but changes entries of recurrent outgoing columns; this intervention is not a function-preserving quotient. Zero forms have both ReLUs OFF.",
    "Near/top-five summaries do not reconstruct all120 scan rows; norm-based dead tests do not prove reachable inactivity. Missing variant driver/raw outcomes/checkpoint hashes remain missing.",
    "Floating exact-mode geometry and fixed numerical cone quadrature do not certify individual leaves or masses. Independent T219 target counts do not transfer those certificates.",
    "For nonnegative normalized joint masses, sum_e max_g p(e,g) is the optimal entire-history classification success from event e. It is not output prediction accuracy or an estimator lower bound.",
    "Entropy effective counts and event-weighted99% covers are not worst-event or computational lower bounds.",
    "Missing SX and id-to-history arrays prevent reconstructing the sign0 variant; numeric IDs do not identify signs.",
    "Checker uses exact stored-float unsigned mass grouping and cover thresholds, independent entropy decomposition and iid strict-order permutation marginals. Signed/nonfinite/malformed outcomes remain explicit; signed masses invalidate probability interpretation.",
    "Paired MC summary mean/second-moment constraints are arithmetic consistency only, not reconstruction of outcomes or confidence coverage."
  ],
